  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> be the side of the regular hexagon<br /><br />Now, for the equilateral triangle <math><mi>F</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo></math> we have<br /><br /><math><mi>O</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math><br /><br />Hence, area of circle,&nbsp;<math><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math> meters ... <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/aavfzumnxiatvzharkujlhndtwikoxlrqhehyrzwtqvfmkocuo.png\" /><br /><br />In right-angled triangle <math><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo></math> right angled at <math><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo></math> we have<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> meters<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Height of the tower <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> meters.",
